The licence above covers this repository's own files: the program around the
emulator (waterbox/, except waterbox/link.cpp and link.h, which are adapted
from Gearlynx's libretro link cable and are under its GPL 3 or later), the tests (including the test program that
tests/make-testprog.py writes) and the documents.

It does not cover Gearlynx. Gearlynx (extern/Gearlynx, a submodule) is
Ignacio Sanchez's Atari Lynx emulator, under the GNU General Public License,
version 3 or later (extern/Gearlynx/LICENSE). It carries miniz, which reads
zip files, under the MIT licence (in its source file). Any file under
patches/ is a change to Gearlynx and is under the GPL 3 or later as well.

The built package, gearlynx.chimeraCore, holds Gearlynx compiled together
with this repository's program, and is distributed under the GNU General
Public License version 3 or later. It holds no boot ROM and no game. The
Lynx's boot ROM is the user's to bring; the 51 bytes of it Gearlynx carried
(the public key that decrypts a cartridge's loader) are read from the
user's boot ROM instead (patches/0002).

The photograph in pictures/ is in the public domain (pictures/*.txt).
